      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Actually, I find it useful at times. Such as when using a pen in VR (I use Oculus Rift DK2 without any controllers. Just HMD + Mouse&Keyboard)\n\nWhilst yes, I do find it's annoying at times, especially when you're talking and trying to change avatar (Holding 'V' to talk in menu sets your cursor in VRChat to the HMD's center, which is a pain when trying to change avatar and you're scrolling through the list. It gets very messy).\n\nI think a toggle for this would be nice.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-22T23:02:36.096Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some setups have a headset but no hand tracking. In that case the user can still use the mouse+keyboard but interaction is locked to the center of the HMD. It would be nice if, like in the HUD menu, the mouse and HMD can be controlled separately. Grabbing, aiming objects could be manipulated by the mouse without having to look in the direction of the object.",
